readExcelFile [SimTalk]
Imports data from the designated Excel file (*.xls) into the list or table designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The method applies to the objects DataStack, DataQueue, DataList, DataTable, and TimeSequence.
Plant Simulation overwrites any existing data.
Plant Simulation does not overwrite the column index and/or the row index of the Plant Simulation
DataTable if the respective Excel cells are empty. To overwrite the contents of the column index and/or the
row index in the Plant Simulation DataTable, delete this content before importing the Excel data.
Note
Plant Simulation uses Excel as COM-server when reading and writing MS Excel-files. For this reason MS
Excel has to be installed on your computer. To continue using the previous, no longer supported Excel
interface, you can use the start option -NativeExcel.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.readExcelFile(FileName:string[, Sheet:string, 
NoDebugger:boolean:=false, Password:string]) → boolean
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter FileName of data type string designates the path to and the name of the Excel file (*.xls).
• The optional parameter Sheet of data type string designates the worksheet. If you do not specify it and if
the Excel file has more than one worksheets, Plant Simulation opens a dialog allowing you to select the
desired worksheet.
• The optional parameter NoDebugger of data type boolean sets if the Method Debugger opens after an
unsuccessful access (false) or not true.
If you do not specify this parameter, the Method Debugger always opens.
If you type in true, the Method Debugger does not open and the method returns the value false when
an error occurs.
Default Value of the Parameter
readExcelFile [SimTalk]
11-4030 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

The default value is false.
• The optional parameter Password of data type string designates the password.
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Example
MyDataList.readExcelFile("C:\users\johnE\times.xls")
MyDataTable.readExcelFile("C:\temp\product_plan.xls","plant xy anytown")
if MyDataStack.readExcelFile("C:\temp\data.xls", true) = false 
   // could not read file
end
