readFile [SimTalk] - lists
Imports data from the designated file into the list or table designated by <Path>. Plant Simulation
overwrites any existing data.
Remarks
The method readFile can import text files, which you exported with the method writeFile, as well as object
files, which you exported with the method writeObjectFile.
The method applies to the objects DataStack, DataQueue, DataList, DataTable, and TimeSequence.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.readFile(FileName:string[, NoDebugger:boolean:=false, 
CodePage:string:="ANSI"]) → boolean
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter FileName of data type string designates the path to and the name of the text file (*.txt).
• The optional parameter NoDebugger of data type boolean sets if the Method Debugger opens after an
unsuccessful access (false) or not true.
Do not specify this parameter to always open the Method Debugger .
Specify true to not open the Method Debugger and to make the method return the value false when an
error occurs.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is false.
• The optional parameter CodePage of data type string sets the encoding you want to use.
You can specify "ANSI" or "System", "UTF-8", or "Unicode".
Do not specify this parameter to use the default encoding ANSI.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is "ANSI".
readFile [SimTalk] - lists
11-4032 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Example
MyDataList.readFile("C:\users\johnE\times.txt")
MyDataTable.readFile("C:\temp\product_plan.psobj")
if MyDataStack.readFile("C:\temp\data.txt", true) = false 
   // could not read file
end
