readXMLFile [SimTalk]
Imports data from the designated XML file (*.xml) into the list/table designated by <Path>. Plant
Simulation overwrites any data that this file might already contain.
Remarks
Note
When reading an XML file that does not use our proprietary format, but Plant Simulation tries to
construct a list/table from any XML data contained in the specified file. For complex XML files some XML
data might not be entirely imported.
If you need to read complex XML files, use the XMLInterface instead.
The method applies to the objects DataStack, DataQueue, DataList, DataTable, and TimeSequence.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.readXMLFile(FileName:string[, NoDebugger:boolean:=false]) → boolean
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter FileName of data type string designates the path to and the name of the XML file
(*.xml).
• The optional parameter NoDebugger of data type boolean sets if the Method Debugger opens after an
unsuccessful access (false) or not true.
If you do not specify this parameter, the Method Debugger always opens.
Specify true to not open the Method Debugger and to return the value false when an error occurs.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is false.
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
readXMLFile [SimTalk]
11-4034 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Example
MyDataTable.readXMLFile("D:\MyName\Public\xmltest.xml")
