writeExcelFile [SimTalk]
Exports the contents of the list/table designated by <Path> to the designated Excel file.
Remarks
Plant Simulation overwrites any existing content and the format of the Excel file.
The method applies to the objects DataStack, DataQueue, DataList, DataTable, and TimeSequence.
Note
Plant Simulation uses Excel as COM-server when reading and writing MS Excel-files. For this reason MS
Excel has to be installed on your computer. To continue using the previous, no longer supported Excel
interface, you can use the start option -NativeExcel.
Note
If you defined a background color in the Plant Simulation DataTable, Plant Simulation writes this
background color to the Excel file. If this is not the case and if the contents of the Plant Simulation
DataTable is written to an existing Excel file, its background color is not altered.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.writeExcelFile(FileName:string[, Sheet:string, 
NoDebugger:boolean=false]) → boolean
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter FileName of data type string designates the Excel file into which Plant Simulation exports
the data.
The file name has to have one of the following extensions: .xls, .xlsx, .xlsm, or .xlsb. The file extension
determines which Excel file format Plant Simulation writes.
• The optional parameter Sheet of data type string designates the worksheet. If you do not type it in, Plant
Simulation saves the list with the name of the worksheet, as Table1.
• The optional parameter NoDebugger of data type boolean sets if the Method Debugger opens after an
unsuccessful access (false) or not true.
Do not specify this parameter to always open the Method Debugger .
writeExcelFile [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-4037
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Specify true to not open the Method Debugger and to return the value false when an error occurs.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is false.
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Example
MyDataStack.writeExcelFile("C:\users\nelly\factory_a.xls")
MyDataTable.writeExcelFile("C:\temp\factory_a.xls","Engines",true)
if MyDataList.writeExcelFile("C:\temp\data.xls") 
   // data written successfully
else // take appropriate measures
end
SimTalk
