writeExcelXMLFile [SimTalk]
Exports the contents of the list/table designated by <Path> to the designated Excel file in Microsoft Excel
Spreadsheet 2003-Format.
Remarks
The method applies to the objects DataStack, DataQueue, DataList, DataTable, and TimeSequence.
Plant Simulation overwrites any existing content of the file.
Note
As opposed to the method writeExcelFile Plant Simulation does not need a Microsoft Excel Installation
on your computer. For this reason writeExcelXMLFile is considerably faster than writeExcelFile.
Note
If you defined a background color in the Plant Simulation DataTable, Plant Simulation writes this
background color to the Excel file. If this is not the case and if the contents of the Plant Simulation
DataTable is written to an existing Excel file, its background color is not altered.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.writeExcelXMLFile(FileName:string[, Sheet:string, 
NoDebugger:boolean:=false]) → boolean
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter FileName of data type string designates the Excel file into which Plant Simulation exports
the data.
The file name has to have the extension xml.
• The optional parameter Sheet of data type string designates the worksheet. If you do not enter it, Plant
Simulation saves the list with the name of the worksheet, as Table1.
• The optional parameter NoDebugger of data type boolean sets if the Method Debugger opens after an
unsuccessful access (false) or not true.
If you do not specify this parameter, the Method Debugger always opens.
writeExcelXMLFile [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-4039
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Specify true to not open Method Debugger and to return the value false when an error occurs.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is false.
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Example
MyDataStack.writeExcelXMLFile("C:\users\nelly\factory_a.xml")
MyDataTable.writeExcelXMLFile("C:\temp\factory_a.xml","Engines",true)
if MyDataList.writeExcelXMLFile("C:\temp\data.xml") 
   // data written successfully
else // take appropriate measures
end
