writeObjectFile [SimTalk]
Exports data of the list/table designated by <Path> to the designated file of type .pslist.
Remarks
Plant Simulation overwrites any data that this file might already contain.
The method applies to the objects DataStack, DataQueue, DataList, DataTable, and TimeSequence.
Type
Method
Syntax
<Path>.writeObjectFile(FileName:string[, NoDebugger:boolean:=false]) → 
boolean
Parameters
You can specify the following parameters:
• The parameter FileName of data type string designates the name of the object file of data type .pslist
into which Plant Simulation exports the data.
Plant Simulation saves the file either to the current folder, compare setCurrentDirectory or to the folder
which you pass as the absolute path.
• The optional parameter NoDebugger of data type boolean sets if the Method Debugger opens after an
unsuccessful access (false) or not true.
If you do not specify this parameter, the Method Debugger always opens.
Specify true to not open the Method Debugger and to return the value false when an error occurs.
Default Value of the Parameter
The default value is false.
Return Value
The return value has the data type boolean.
Example
MyDataStack.writeObjectFile("C:\users\johnE\times.pslist")
MyDataTable.writeObjectFile("C:\temp\run1.pslist")
if MyDataList.writeObjectFile("C:\temp\data.pslist", true) 
